the hug they've been waiting for for two  months grandfather and granddaughter  reunited during the quarantine we were  desperate now I can't even speak for how  excited I am too excited we have only  seen her with video calls for two months  but it was not the same it couldn't be  the same  Randall avi stylophora when I saw her my  heart stopped it seemed to be a century  since I'd seen her after the longest  lockdown in Europe family visits are  allowed but only if relatives live in  the same region elsewhere the queues  were back at Rome's main determining  station though it's not just tickets but  temperatures being taken obviously after  staying at home for almost 60 days it  feels good I feel good and I feel safe  across Italy more than four million  people were back at work as construction  sites and factories reopened and  restaurants were allowed to sell  takeaway food but taking public  transport is still being discouraged by  government and masks a compulsory when  sharing public spaces and doors funerals  remain limited to 15 people but the  bereaved are able to leave flowers on  the graves of the dead the florists  nearby carefully disinfected with more  than 210,000 reported cases and around  29,000 deaths  Italy's one of the worst affected  countries government leaders fear the  loosening of restrictions will lead to a  resurgence and cases health care workers  are taking extra measures to track  infections isolate clusters and make  sure hospitals aren't overwhelmed again  we're being careful trying not to do too  many things but at least we're finally  outside and breathing some fresh air  families making the most of the sunshine  and parks that have been reopened though  playgrounds remain off-limits  you're happy because finally today they  have opened Fila Borghese after having  closed it for a month and a half  even though obviously my daughter was  disappointed to find the playground all  blocked off  there are many reminders that life isn't  t